index 5205525..9d6fc45 100644
--- a/docs/agents/sessions.md
+++ b/docs/agents/sessions.md
@@ -1,5 +1,11 @@
 # Sessions, branching and live events
 
+## Local Review Companion sidebar patch
+
+`ReviewCompanionPanel` is a right-panel view beside file/terminal tabs. It is keyed by the selected session and unmounts while hidden, so stale requests cannot retain another session's iframe. Its endpoint reads only the active session's `review-companion-pi.bridges.v2` entry; it never starts a model, restores an idle session, or creates a review. A closed/absent wrapper returns an unavailable state and the panel retries while visible.
+
+The local CLI supplies `REVIEW_COMPANION_EMBED_ORIGIN` from its exact loopback host and port. Companion 0.3.6 opts into that one `frame-ancestors` source for Web mode only. Pi Web's existing request/Host/password protection still gates the discovery endpoint; tokens stay in the iframe URL fragment and are not logged. This is a same-machine integration, not a remote proxy. Review uses copy-and-paste; it does not alter the chat draft or send a prompt.
+
 ## AgentSession lifecycle (`lib/rpc-manager.ts`)
 - One `AgentSessionWrapper` per session id in `globalThis.__piSessions` (`globalThis` survives Next.js hot reload; a module-level Map does not). Concurrent `startRpcSession()` calls share one start Promise (`globalThis.__piStartLocks`). Idle timeout: 10 minutes (`PI_WEB_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS`, `0` disables).
 - Stop cannot cancel a run awaiting a promise that ignores the abort signal (a third-party extension handler or tool): `inner.abort()` never returns. So Stop (`abort`, `abort_bash`) sets `forceShutdownOnIdle` and arms the idle timer, shutting the wrapper down one idle timeout after the first Stop even while it runs. Later commands (a reload's `get_tools`, Stop again) must not push that deadline back; with `PI_WEB_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=0` it still arms, at 10 minutes.
